-- title:
--   Integral j-charts surject onto the Igusa curve charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\neq 0$ with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ over $L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the image under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$, and let $j\in K$ be non-zero with Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$ under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, and let $w$ be an `IntegralWeightOneForm` for $k$ and $M$: a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$, a power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ which is an integral $q$-expansion of it, and the requirement that the associated series `intSeriesC` over $k$ be non-zero. Write $\mathcal{I}=$ [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) for the resulting intermediate field of $k((q))$ over $k$, and $A_{\mathrm{fin}}=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, $A_\infty=$ `chartAlgInf A K j` for the two $A$-subalgebras of $K$ attached to $\{j\}$ and $\{j^{-1}\}$. Then there exist $t\in\mathcal{I}$ and $k$-algebra homomorphisms $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}\colon k\otimes_A A_{\mathrm{fin}}\to$ `chartRing k {t}` and $\theta_\infty\colon k\otimes_A A_\infty\to$ `chartRing k {t⁻¹}` — the targets being the elements of $\mathcal{I}$ integral over $k[t]$, respectively over $k[t^{-1}]$ — such that: the Laurent expansion of $t$ is [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $=q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$ over $k$; both $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\theta_\infty$ are surjective; $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}(1\otimes j)=t$ and $\theta_\infty(1\otimes j^{-1})=t^{-1}$; whenever $b\in A_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $b'\in A_\infty$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$ satisfy $b=b'j^n$ in $K$, one has $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}(1\otimes b)=\theta_\infty(1\otimes b')\,t^n$; for $b$ in either chart algebra and $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ non-zero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $b\cdot y=x$ as Laurent series over $L$, the Laurent expansion of the image of $1\otimes b$ is $\bar{x}/\bar{y}$ over $k$; and the kernel of each of $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}},\theta_\infty$ is the ideal generated by the elements of the form $1\otimes b$ that it kills.
--
--   This identifies the reduction of the two integral $j$-charts of the model of $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_1(p))$ over $A$ along the multiplicative branch with the two affine charts of the Igusa curve in characteristic $p$, in the form of surjections of $k$-algebras reading off Gauss reductions of $q$-expansions. It is used in the construction of closed immersions of the pair of charts into the special fibre of the two-chart integral model.
